                <pb facs="0826" n="814" sameAs="frus:frus1939v01/pg814"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">300.115(39)/311: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1939-12-16T13:00:00+00:00">December 16,
                            1939—1 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received December 16—8:30 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2647. Department’s 1609, December 15. London representative Lykes Brothers
                    advises that <hi rendition="#italic">Winston Salem</hi> was released under
                    so-called “Black Diamond” guarantee, namely that the company would return the
                    cotton to British port at their expense but not in the <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Winston Salem</hi>; in fact the cotton is now unloaded on the dock at
                    Rotterdam and it is planned to send the <hi rendition="#italic">Winston
                        Salem</hi> direct to the United States and to return the cotton to British
                    port by coastal steamer. In view of this, will not approach British authorities
                    with regard to <hi rendition="#italic">Winston Salem</hi> and will await further
                    instructions. Is it desired to make separate inquiry with regard to seizure of
                    the cotton?</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
